    {
      "id": "2071073620567150619",
      "text": "Every time a new tool drops, the same debate fires up.\n\n\"Is this the death of After Effects?\"\n\nIt never is.\n\nFigma Motion looks clean. But calling it an AE killer tells me you've never storyboarded a 3 minute VSL by hand. Never built sound design from scratch. Never paced a cut to match a voiceover breath.\n\nI said this last week about AI video tools and I'll say it again. Everyone's chasing the new thing. Very few are learning how to actually edit.\n\nThe tool is never the bottleneck. Taste is. And taste takes years of reps, not a new UI.\n\nSoftware changes every year. The editors who understand story don't flinch.",
      "author": {
        "id": "1780830569393512448",
        "name": "Tipra",
        "screenName": "Tipra_",
        "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1993558188093022208/8Fp8-BcH_normal.jpg",
